       "en": "Valuation: all companies use the same forward P/E scale. A P/E of 10× scores 9, 20× scores 7, 30× scores 5, 40× scores 3, and 55× or higher scores 0. When any company in the comparison has no forward P/E (for example, it is loss-making), every company is compared on price-to-sales instead (market value ÷ the last four quarters' revenue): 1× scores 9, 2× scores 7, 4× scores 5, 8× scores 3, 16× scores 1, and 23× or higher scores 0. This isn't a ranking against peers or an estimate of fair value. Earnings at the peak of a business cycle aren't adjusted to a normal level."
